<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calcŭlōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		calculus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Full of small stones</i> or <i>pebbles</i>, <i>stony</i>, <i>pebbly</i>, <i>gravelly</i> (post - Aug.): pomum,
			Cloat. ap. <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 15, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					Arb. 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 11, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 14, 49, § 170</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Afficted with calculus</i> or <i>stone</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 7, 26</span></i>, n. 2; <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 4,
				9, § 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib.
				Comp. 150</span></i> and 153; <i><span class="en">Veg. 2,
			18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
